# Database Changes — Mandatory Compliance

> **STOP.** Before any database work, read and follow:
> `.cursor/skills/database-change/SKILL.md`
> `.cursor/architecture/DATABASE-CHANGE-CHECKLIST.md`

## Trigger — This Rule Applies When You

- Create, alter, or drop a migration
- Add/remove/modify a column, index, FK, or constraint
- Create or modify an Eloquent model schema
- Improve database performance (indexes, partitioning)
- Update `database-blueprint.md`

## Mandatory Workflow (No Skipping)

```
1. READ  database-blueprint.md        → table must exist or be added first
2. READ  01-principles-and-layers.md  → data types, temporal rules
3. READ  indexing-matrix.md           → if indexes involved
4. FILL  DATABASE-CHANGE-CHECKLIST.md → every checkbox
5. WRITE migration + model
6. UPDATE database-blueprint.md       → ALWAYS sync reference
7. UPDATE indexing-matrix.md          → if indexes changed
8. VERIFY migrate up + rollback
```

## Hard Rules

- Migration only — never manual production SQL
- `$table->id()` (BIGINT) — never UUID as internal PK unless blueprint says so
- `smallInteger` for status — never `tinyInteger`
- FK: `->constrained()->restrictOnDelete()` — never cascade on academic tables
- Index every FK column used in queries
- `academic_year_id` on all academic transactional tables
- Never hard-delete academic history — use status + effective_to
- Blueprint MUST be updated after every schema change

## If Blueprint and Request Conflict

Stop and ask the user. Do not invent schema. Blueprint is the source of truth unless user explicitly approves deviation (then update blueprint first).

